# Preserve original audio, cinematics, localization, UI, mission, and tuning…

Preserve original audio, cinematics, localization, UI, mission, and tuning
data in deterministic normalized forms.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Preserve original audio, cinematics, localization, UI, mission, and tuning
  data in deterministic normalized forms; keep English as canonical base input
  and preserve other official languages as deterministic language-mod sources.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

The faithful extraction pipeline remains nine base-only stages. It normalizes
RSD audio to WAV, extracts RCF archives, and converts supported RMV/Bink movies
to HAP video plus one PCM WAV per source audio stream. Movie stream order is
preserved as `audio_track_01.wav`, `audio_track_02.wav`, and so on; the current
normalized movie tree contains 16 English track-01 packages and eight packages
each carrying localized tracks 02, 03, and 04.

Canonical non-English localization is now internal Rust product code under
`src/localization/languages/`. The original PC/PAL runtime evidence maps
French/German/Spanish
FMV audio indexes 1/2/3 to normalized tracks 02/03/04 after the English index-0
track. Language composition also preserves the exact TextBible table/sidecar,
matching dialogue RCF, localized loading/license UI assets, optional localized
readme, SHA-256 evidence, and UTF-8 text records. The current lawful source has
21 localized loading/license assets for each of French/German/Spanish and real
dialogue archives for all three. Eleven external Rust integration tests cover
all three cinematic-track mappings, fail-closed missing UI/dialogue/cinematic
audio, fail-closed Italian placeholder-only source, source-root read-only
containment, byte-deterministic repeated output, normalized mod-package
publication, and manifest/report serialization agreement.

Italian remains intentionally unavailable from the current source: all 1,632
Italian text records are `???`, `dialogi.rcf` is absent, and no Italian
localized
loading/license assets are present. No content is synthesized to fill those
gaps.

The shared normalized SHAR mod-package contract now backs canonical language
publication directly, and the language domain is separated from filesystem,
serialization, hashing, and package-publication composition. This parent task
remains open because broader mission/tuning preservation and final release
integration still require their own end-to-end evidence. Language mods are not
inserted as a tenth faithful-base extraction stage and do not alter base-game
identity.
